    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 270 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the sequential membership number for newly created owners, exposed as the integer field `membershipNumber` in the owner response.\n\n**How the value is assigned:** a new pipeline step counts the existing owners (`ownerRepository.findAll().size()`) and sets `membershipNumber = count + 1` on the owner before it is saved (the owner isn't persisted yet, so it isn't counted). Because the acceptance test runs both creations in one rolled-back transaction, the JPQL count auto-flushes the first insert, so the second owner sees one more existing owner \u2014 giving the exact `a + 1 == b` invariant the test asserts.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` (integer, int32) property to the `Owner` schema; the OpenAPI codegen regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field, and MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the persisted `membershipNumber` field (`membership_number` column) with getter/setter.\n- `rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java` \u2014 new OfficeFloor function that reads the `@Val Owner`, counts owners, and sets the membership number in place.\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `assignMembership` step (governed by `transaction`) between `rejectDuplicateEmail` and `save`.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the nullable `membership_number` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb; existing seed owners keep it null since the rule only applies to newly created owners).\n\nThe value is persisted, so it is returned both on the `POST` create response and on subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads.",
